.venv/
.vscode/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
# The runtime state stays out of the repo (runs.db / datasets.db / cookies / exports),
# but a saved workflow is authored work the user wants versioned — it references datasets
# by id, so a checkout of it is only useful next to the same data/, which is stated in the
# README rather than hidden by an ignore rule.
data/*
!data/workflows/
!data/workflows/**
# The fine-tuned model registry is a name→relative-path map the model picker and docs cite;
# tiny, no secrets — version it so others get the same display names.
!data/model_registry.json
logs/
# `.pylintrc` USED to be ignored here, which is why pylint was never a real review standard:
# the configuration lived on one machine, CI could not read it, and a clone linted nothing.
# The three tier configs (.pylintrc, .pylintrc.tests, .pylintrc.probes) are versioned on purpose.
# backend/test_*.py are one-off measurement PROBES, kept out of git ON PURPOSE: they run against a
# live site with a real cookie and assert nothing, so tracking them would put throwaway scripts in
# CI's `ruff check backend/` and the pytest collection. The 141 that had accumulated were archived
# to F:/python_project/crawls/_archive/backend_probes_2026-10-25.zip and deleted on 2026-10-25; what
# they measured is cited in docs/crawler_notes.md, docs/why_finetuned_bert.md and docs/live_test_plan.md,
# which is the part worth keeping. The rule stays so the next probe is ignored the same way, and it is
# linted locally with `--rcfile=.pylintrc.probes` (never in CI: a runner has none of these files).
backend/test_*.py
.qoder/settings.local.json
.qoder/sessions/
.coverage
htmlcov/

scratchpad/
# Real vendor exports stay on the machine they were downloaded on. Their own files say so:
# the Dimensions download's first row is "Redistribution / external use of this work (or parts
# thereof) is prohibited without prior written approval", and Scopus/WoS licences say the same
# in their terms. The committed fixtures are the synthetic `*_demo.*` files beside these, which
# are written to the *same* column names, tag spellings and separators — so every dialect
# discovered here is still tested, without shipping anyone's data.
samples/CNKI-*
samples/CSSCI.txt
samples/Scopus_*
samples/Dimensions-*
samples/WOS.*
samples/lens-export.csv
samples/pubmed-*
# ml_train holds the fine-tuning workspace. Keep the big/private subdirs out (datasets = crawled
# social content, models = 1.6G weights, logs), but VERSION the scripts + dir-map README so every
# cited accuracy/F1 has its producing code in the repo. These scripts self-locate their sys.path.
ml_train/*
!ml_train/scripts/
!ml_train/README.md
# Project-local pip download cache + build temp (kept off the C: drive on purpose).
.pip-cache/
.tmp/
# Windows desktop build: the build env, PyInstaller work dir and release artifacts are
# reproducible from desktop/ and must never be committed.
build/
dist/
desktop/.venv-build/
desktop/.pyinstaller-cache/
# Pip sometimes falls back to cwd for temporary build dirs on restricted Windows
# sandboxes; these are never source and must not be committed.
pip-build-*/
pip-install-*/
pip-unpack-*/
pip-ephem-wheel-cache-*/
jieba.cache
